WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:16.408
The next morning Dorothy and her friends met in front of the throne room.

2
00:00:16.409 --> 00:00:20.102
Everyone but Dorothy was very excited to see Oz.

3
00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:26.528
"Congratulate me," said the Scarecrow. "Today Oz will give me a brain."

4
00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:31.021
Dorothy looked at her friends and said, "I like you all as you are.

5
00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:35.268
A brain, a heart, and courage cannot change that."

6
00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:38.642
"That is kind of you to say," said the Scarecrow.

7
00:00:38.643 --> 00:00:41.694
"But I would like a brain all the same."

8
00:00:41.695 --> 00:00:45.124
"Shall we go in?" asked the Tin Man.

9
00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:48.181
The Lion knocked on the door of the throne room.

10
00:00:48.182 --> 00:00:50.824
"Come in," called Oz.

11
00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:56.459
They found him sitting at a desk next to the window. He was thinking deeply.

12
00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.656
"I have come for my brain," said the Scarecrow softly.

13
00:01:00.657 --> 00:01:05.384
"Oh yes," said Oz. "Sit down please.

14
00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:08.451
First I must place this hat upon your head.

15
00:01:08.452 --> 00:01:17.205
Okay, with the power vested in me, I confer a doctorate in philosophy from the University of Oz to the Scarecrow.

16
00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:22.663
Congratulations, Scarecrow. Here is your diploma."

17
00:01:22.664 --> 00:01:26.282
"Does this mean I have a brain?" asked the Scarecrow.

18
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.236
"It does indeed," said Oz.

19
00:01:29.237 --> 00:01:34.431
"In fact, your friends should call you Doctor Scarecrow from now on."

20
00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:40.206
The Tin Man stepped forward. "I have come for a heart."

21
00:01:40.207 --> 00:01:47.536
"Very well," said Oz. "But I will have to cut a hole in your chest, and it might hurt."

22
00:01:47.537 --> 00:01:50.866
"I'm not worried about that," said the Tin Man.

23
00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:53.676
"I can bear any amount of pain for a heart."

24
00:01:53.677 --> 00:02:00.283
Oz took a pair of tin shears from his desk and cut a square hole in the Tin Man's chest.

25
00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:06.253
He put a small, heart-shaped clock inside the Tin Man.

26
00:02:06.254 --> 00:02:13.152
"There," said Oz. "You have a heart that any regular man would be proud of."

27
00:02:13.153 --> 00:02:16.590
"Thank you," replied the Tin Man proudly.

28
00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:23.268
The Lion then walked forward and said, "I have come for my courage."

29
00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:28.761
"Here you are," said Oz. He handed a small green bottle to the Lion.

30
00:02:28.762 --> 00:02:31.434
"What is it?" asked the Lion.

31
00:02:31.435 --> 00:02:41.919
"Well, if it were inside you, it would be called courage. Drink it!" said Oz.

32
00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.091
"How do you feel?" asked Oz after the Lion had drunk all the liquid in the bottle.

33
00:02:47.092 --> 00:02:51.272
"Full of courage," roared the Lion.

34
00:02:51.273 --> 00:02:57.008
The Scarecrow, the Tin Man, and the Lion walked out of Oz's throne room proudly.

35
00:02:57.009 --> 00:03:03.943
Dorothy remained behind and asked, "Have you found a way for me to return to Kansas?"

36
00:03:03.944 --> 00:03:06.583
"No," said Oz sadly.

37
00:03:06.584 --> 00:03:13.515
"It was easy to make the Scarecrow, Tin Man, and Lion happy because they believed I could do anything.

38
00:03:13.516 --> 00:03:20.020
But I will need a lot more than my imagination to help you get back to Kansas."

39
00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:25.049
Dorothy stayed with her happy friends while she waited for Oz to think of a plan.

40
00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:30.386
After four days Oz came to her and said, "There might be a way."

41
00:03:30.387 --> 00:03:34.531
"To return to Kansas?" Dorothy asked eagerly.

42
00:03:34.532 --> 00:03:41.467
"Yes," said Oz. "The one major problem for us is getting across the Great Desert.

43
00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:45.411
Once we cross the desert, finding Kansas should be easy.

44
00:03:45.412 --> 00:03:49.100
And I think I know how we can cross the desert."

45
00:03:49.101 --> 00:03:52.113
"How?" asked Dorothy.

46
00:03:52.114 --> 00:03:56.346
"In a hot-air balloon," answered Oz.

47
00:03:56.347 --> 00:04:00.532
"But how will you make it fly?" asked Dorothy.

48
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:05.276
"Well, there are two ways to make a balloon fly," answered Oz.

49
00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:12.037
"With gas or hot air. There isn't any gas in Oz, so we will use hot air."

50
00:04:12.038 --> 00:04:16.165
"We?" asked Dorothy.

51
00:04:16.166 --> 00:04:21.877
"Yes, of course," said Oz. "I can't let you go alone.

52
00:04:21.878 --> 00:04:25.451
But it will take me at least a week to get everything ready.

53
00:04:25.452 --> 00:04:31.197
We are going to need a large balloon made of silk and a giant basket to ride in.

54
00:04:31.198 --> 00:04:35.289
We'll also need a bunch of ropes to tie the balloon to the basket."

55
00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.057
"Can I help?" asked Dorothy.

56
00:04:38.058 --> 00:04:45.618
"If you can sew, you can help to make the balloon," answered Oz.
